  "title": "Long Vowels & First Words",
  "summary": "Stretching vowels with ا و ي and reading real words.",
  "sections": [
    { "type": "text", "body": "<p>A long vowel is a short vowel followed by its matching letter. The letter stretches the sound to about twice as long:</p>" },
    { "type": "table", "headers": ["Example", "Pattern", "Sound"], "arCols": [0], "rows": [
      ["بَا", "fatḥa + alif", "bā (long a, as in father)"],
      ["بِي", "kasra + yāʼ", "bī (long i, as in bee)"],
      ["بُو", "ḍamma + wāw", "bū (long u, as in boot)"]
    ] },
    { "type": "note", "body": "Short vs long changes meaning. Compare <span class='ar' lang='ar' style='font-size:1.5rem'>كَتَبَ</span> kataba (he wrote) with <span class='ar' lang='ar' style='font-size:1.5rem'>كَاتِب</span> kātib (writer)." },
    { "type": "text", "body": "<p>Now read the words below. Cover the transliteration, sound each one out letter by letter, then check yourself and press ▶ to listen.</p>" }
  ],
